Z||000000||Smokey19335||04-04-2001||10:38 PM||||Hi, just found this site, probably a mistake! Here I go again! Owned a 86Gt that I bought used in 88, low mileage, kept it 2 years & sold it to buy my last boat! Big mistake!4speed, black & silver a/c etc & it ran nice, quick! Took it to Pontiac dealer initially to have it checked out & never needed anything after except routine. Think I sold it for 5500.00, can't remember. Think maybe its time for another GT! Didn't realize all the interest in this car! Just like the 57,64ss,69ss,&75z28 that i all should have kept. Anyway, looking forward to learning from this site, some nice looking members cars, and carlisle show is 50 minutes from my house! 2 questions: good places to look for cars for sale, and what is the life expectancy of the 2.8 engine mileage wise & are they expensive to have Pont.Dealer work on? Sorry I rambled, Dave||||reg||10
Z||000001||skitime||04-04-2001||10:46 PM||||Welcome to the forum! You are sort of a neighbor. One of the good places to find a Fiero is <A HREF="http://www.AutoTrader.com" TARGET=_blank>www.AutoTrader.com</A>   Many of us had Fieros that we wished that we had kept.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||04-04-2001||11:01 PM||||I would strongly recommend you go to Carlisle!  Wouldn't be surprised if you bought a Fiero the next day or even at the show!  To check out cars for sale try <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com" TARGET=_blank>www.classifieds2000.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.cars.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cars.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.autotrader.com" TARGET=_blank>www.autotrader.com</A>  like prebviously mentioned.  <P><BR>About the 2.8, I think it can be reliable if you baby it, keep up with oil changes, don't drive it like a race car, you should have no problem.  But it does have bottem end oiling issues so the oil change thing is a biggie especially with 100k+ mile engines.  When my 2.8 spun a bearing I decided to replace it with a 3.4 because it only costed about $200 more for the 3.4 and you not only gain Hp and Torque you gain reliability of a stronger block.  <P>just my 2 cents <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||6
Z||000003||Black88GT||04-04-2001||11:01 PM||||first double post, DOH!<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 04-04-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-04-2001||11:48 PM||||103,000mi on my factory 2.8  It rattles, and smokes at higher rpm's, but it's also had 30+ bottles on nitrous through it, numberous dyno floggings, and countless a$$-whoopings from both previous owner and myself.  This car is living proof that the 2.8 takes abuse as long as it's treated to fresh oil.||||reg||1
